      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/NET0007", "Net-(J9-Pin_2)", "GND"],
      "observed": "J6.2 is connected to ESP32 GPIO1 and the high-side switch control pins U5.1 (IN) and U5.2 (DIAG_EN); J6.1 is GND. The switch output U5.7 instead connects to J9.2, whose other pin J9.1 is GND.",
      "expected": "The specification says the high-side switch OUT feeds heater connector J6 pin 2. J6.2 should therefore connect to the switch output, not to GPIO1 and the switch control inputs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0007\") ... (node (ref \"J6\") (pin \"2\")) ... (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\")) ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"Net-(J9-Pin_2)\") (node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J6\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A heater connected to the specified J6 connector would be driven directly from GPIO1 rather than the protected 12 V switch output, risking GPIO overload and preventing normal heater operation. The switched output is routed to J9 instead.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The heater output is not connected to the specified J6 connector: J6.2 is on the GPIO1/control net, while the high-side switch output is routed to J9. This would make the documented heater connection behave incorrectly and could overload the MCU GPIO."
}

